From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: App Control Center, Freezer and Student mode model

Pure Java next to the 1101 model, with host tests (tests/sable-apps,
AppControlCenterModelTest):

* AppSuspensions: Freezer, Student mode and Focus mode share Android's
  one suspension per suspending package, so they share one target set
  (strongest reason FROZEN > STUDENT > FOCUS). An app is released only
  when no control wants it; Focus mode ending never unfreezes an app,
  and only Settings' own suspensions are released.
* StudentSchedule: days, start and end (overnight windows run into the
  next day), isActive and nextChange for the alarm, a damage-tolerant
  stored form (default weekdays 08:00-17:00), and the blocked set
  (launcher apps not on the allow list and not ones the phone needs).
* AppControlRows: per-app network, background and paused state from
  Android's own stores, the list filters, and the hide rule (only
  frozen, user-installed apps the phone does not need).
---
